        "type": "answer",
        "id": "r0c0",
        "text": "A heat pump moves heat from outside to inside using a refrigerant that changes between liquid and gas. First, the refrigerant absorbs heat from the outside air, even on a cold day.\nA compressor then squeezes the refrigerant, which heats it up.\nIn the condenser, the hot refrigerant gives its heat to your home.\nAn expansion valve then lowers its pressure, so it cools and the cycle starts again.\n",
